/* rtx.gbuffer.slimVariants: the RayQuery G-buffer kernels (gbuffer_rayquery.comp.slang) with features the frame cannot
   use compiled out. Each WBOIT feature set below has a primary and a PSR pass:
     psr_prepare                   without NRC
     psr_prepare_stochastic_alpha  without NRC, with rtx.enableStochasticAlphaBlend
     psr_inline                    with NRC
     psr_inline_stochastic_alpha   with NRC and rtx.enableStochasticAlphaBlend
   Levels, picked per frame by DxvkPathtracerGbuffer::selectSlimLevel:
     slim     GBUFFER_SLIM_NO_POM + GBUFFER_SLIM_NO_THIN_FILM + GBUFFER_SLIM_NO_PORTALS
     lean     slim + GBUFFER_SLIM_NO_SSS
     slimpom  slim with POM kept
     leanpom  lean with POM kept
   The host binds a level only while the compiled-out branches cannot run in that frame, so the output is the same.
   Stochastic alpha uses the same predicates, since it reads none of what a slim axis removes. It reads only the opaque
   interaction's opacity, albedo and shading normal, the surface hash and the hit distance, and only POM changes the
   shading normal. */

//!variant gbuffer_rayquery_psr_prepare_wboit_slim.comp
//!>       RAY_TRACING_PRIMARY_RAY ATMOSPHERE_AVAILABLE
//!>       GBUFFER_FEATURE_DLSSRR=1 GBUFFER_FEATURE_OBJECT_PICKING=0 GBUFFER_FEATURE_RAYTRACED_RENDER_TARGET=0 GBUFFER_FEATURE_STOCHASTIC_ALPHA=0
//!>       GBUFFER_FEATURE_PSR_REPLACEMENT=1 GBUFFER_FEATURE_INLINE_PSR_SAMPLING=0
//!>       UNORDERED_RESOLVE_WBOIT
//!>       GBUFFER_SLIM_NO_POM GBUFFER_SLIM_NO_THIN_FILM GBUFFER_SLIM_NO_PORTALS

//!variant gbuffer_rayquery_psr_prepare_wboit_lean.comp
//!>       RAY_TRACING_PRIMARY_RAY ATMOSPHERE_AVAILABLE
